// Assigning to a top-level variable from a function is refused for the same
// reason reading one is, and says the same thing: the name is a local of the
// program body. A `const` would not help here -- a constant cannot be
// assigned either -- but the message is about what the name IS, which is
// what the reader has got wrong.
int count = 0;

void bump() {
    count = count + 1;
}

bump();
print(count);
